#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
Configurable-OD Value Reader
----------------------------
Reads every configurable Object Dictionary entry from the AMR chassis (Kinco
FD12X/FD1X4S, nodes 1-6 on can0) and the liftkit (Kinco FD1X5, node 7 on can1)
over expedited SDO and prints them in a tabular, tier-tagged report.

Object set mirrors `actuator_od_configurable_risk_register.md` — the same
FATAL / PERSISTENT / TUNING / COMMS taxonomy, so a row here maps 1:1 to a row
there. Pure read-only telemetry (statusword, actual pos/vel/current, temps) is
intentionally excluded; it is not configurable and changes with drive state.

IMPORTANT: run at PRE-FLIGHT, before the ros2_canopen stack starts. The runtime
driver reprograms the PDO map (0x1400-0x1BFF), the heartbeat consumer (0x1016)
and 0x6007 at activation, so those only read the saved EEPROM config while the
stack is down.

Bus / node map (from SDO.md + liftkit_bus.yml):
  can0 : AMR — travel wheel_f=1 wheel_rl=3 wheel_rr=5 (Profile Velocity);
               steer steering_f=2 steering_rl=4 steering_rr=6 (Profile Position)
  can1 : liftkit node 7  (tool node 8 is a CiA-301 I/O device — no config OD)

Usage:
  ./read_od_values                       # AMR (can0) + liftkit (can1)
  ./read_od_values --amr-only
  ./read_od_values --lift-only
  ./read_od_values --nodes 2 4 6         # subset of AMR nodes
  ./read_od_values --amr-iface can0 --lift-iface can1
  ./read_od_values --hex                 # values in hex as well as decimal
"""

